You are working on AI-EMS v5.1, an agentic AI prototype for power system EMS.

LANGUAGE POLICY:
- Code identifiers (variables, functions, classes): English (PEP 8)
- Comments, docstrings, CLAUDE.md, design docs: Korean
- This .cursorrules file: English (Cursor IDE compatibility)
- AI agent responses to user: Korean
- If CLAUDE.md and this file conflict, CLAUDE.md takes precedence.

CRITICAL RULES:
- Never generate numerical values from LLM. All numbers must come from pandapower solvers.
- Redis ops: namespace is WRITE-PROTECTED. Only SCADA simulator writes to ops:.
- All API responses must use Pydantic v2 schemas.
- Every AI response must include snapshot_ts and evidence_chain.
- study: namespace TTL 1800s auto-delete mandatory.

V5.1 MDP FOCUS (Phase 1):
- Korean real grid .raw file → pandapower from_psse() → runpp() convergence
- 4 EMS stubs: TP, SE, CA, SCA (FastAPI + Pydantic)
- Redis ops: 4-second SCADA simulation cycle
- Proactive AI Insights deferred to Phase 4

TECH STACK: Python 3.11, FastAPI, PydanticAI v0.7+, pandapower 3.x, Redis 7.x,
PostgreSQL 16+TimescaleDB, Streamlit 1.x, MapLibre GL JS, Chroma+BGE-M3

DOMAIN: Korean power system (산업통상자원부고시 제2023-65호).
Voltage in pu. Targets: 345kV ±5%, 154kV 95~105%, 66kV 97~103%. Operating range: ±10%.
Frequency 60Hz (±0.2Hz normal per 고시 제4조). Min: 59.7Hz(single fault), 59.5Hz(cascading).
Power in MW/Mvar. N-1 criterion mandatory (고시 제15조).
Fault clearing: 345kV 4cycles(66.7ms), 154kV 5cycles(83.3ms).
Refer to docs/domain/glossary.json for Korean power terminology.

POWER DOMAIN RULES:
- pandapower solver returned values only. LLM numerical generation = forbidden
- Voltage always in pu. Power in MW/Mvar. Frequency in Hz
- Redis ops: write code forbidden except SCADA simulator
- study: namespace TTL 1800s auto-delete mandatory
- Power flow divergence → return solved=false + message, never None

CODE QUALITY RULES:
- All API endpoints require Pydantic v2 input/output schemas
- All functions require type hints. Optional explicit
- FastAPI routers use APIRouter() separation
- Tests: test_ file required per module. pytest used
- Logging: print() forbidden → structlog (JSON structured logs)
- Error handling: bare except forbidden. Use specific exception types

WHEN WRITING PYDANTICAI AGENTS:
- Use @agent.tool decorator for tool registration
- Use RunContext[AgentContext] for context passing
- Set result_type to typed Pydantic model
- Include Korean power terms in system prompts
- evidence_chain always appended with Tool call records
- HITL required → set requires_hitl=True field

WHEN WRITING FASTAPI STUBS:
- Use APIRouter() for route separation
- Return Pydantic models (never raw dicts)
- Include error cases (solved=false, not None)
- Add structlog logging to every endpoint

FORBIDDEN PATTERNS:
- Redis pickle serialization → JSON only
- Global variable state management → Redis or function params
- Hardcoded voltage/current thresholds → voltage_limits.json reference
- LLM prompt direct numerical insertion → Tool result reference
- time.sleep() → asyncio.sleep() or APScheduler
